<title>UK: Fannie Mae prices $500 mln 5-year global bonds.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae prices $500 mln 5-year global bonds.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal National Mortgage Association (Fannie Mae) has priced its $500 million five-year global bond due January 16, 2002, joint lead managers Merrill Lynch and Lehman Brothers said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The bonds will have a coupon of 6.375 percent and an issue and reoffer price of 99.852 to yield 10 basis points over the five-year U.S. Treasury note.</p>
<p>The payment date will be on January 16, it said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7658</p>
